 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Their claim «هؤلاء شفعاؤنا عند الله» is framed («قولا خاليا من البرهان»); 18:1-9 is not glossed (As-Sa'di's «مثقال ذرة» is a Quran phrase). No idols drawn. As-Sa'di's first-person «ننجي… ونهلك» is not used. The hourglass in 20 leaves before the Prophet's ﷺ «إني معكم من المنتظرين». STAGING v4: c1 (18) is staged in a town by day: two small groups of three idolaters (dark robes, countable, never behind rocks) face each other (the second walks in on 18:1); the left group says their claim on 18:10 and the right group answers on 18:12, each toward the other (the claim is framed by the red gloss). No idol, statue or worship is drawn, nobody points (18:11 is a demonstrative) and nobody turns toward an empty side. The reply 18:15-25 is commanded to the Prophet: camera only, no gesture. A geometric plate on 18:26 (His transcendence), the camera closes on the idolaters on 18:28. c2 (19) is staged in the same town: two small groups of plain people; the right group joins the left on 19:3 (one community, both tafsirs) and walks apart on 19:7 (they differed: some disbelieved, some held to the truth, Al-Muyassar); an hourglass plate for the respite (19:8, gone before 19:12); nothing happens on the counterfactual judgement (19:13-14, camera wide); on 19:15-17 the left group speaks toward the right group, which shakes its head (they differ). c3 (20) stays ambient: their demand concerns the Prophet and 20:8-16 are his commanded words; quiet over them. The cover now shows the idolaters' claim (18:12)."
 },
